@baseUrl = http://localhost:5181
@landlordEmail = <disposable-landlord-a-email>
@landlordPassword = <set-a-local-test-password>
@landlordBEmail = <disposable-landlord-b-email>
@investorEmail = <disposable-unapproved-investor-email>
@landlordToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@landlordBToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@investorToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@approvedInvestorToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@adminToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@landId = <land-id-from-create>
@draftLandId = <a-second-draft-land-id>
@documentId = <document-id-from-upload>

# How these results were produced (read this before trusting a PASS):
# - The requests below were NOT sent through this file in an HTTP client. Each case
#   was executed as an equivalent request by a PowerShell driver
#   (%TEMP%\opencode\s4_tests.ps1 and s4_regression.ps1) against the running app.
#   The method, path, body and expected status are the same; the driver is the evidence.
# - Result legend, on the line under each case title:
#   PASS     executed by the driver; the actual status matched the expectation
#   FAIL     executed; the actual status did not match (none in the last full run,
#            including the post-remediation rerun; see docs/tests/security-step4.http)
#   BLOCKED  not executed here. The S4-50..S4-62 admin cases in this file were BLOCKED
#            until the approved C1 admin recovery: NEBRASDB_Step1's only SuperAdmin was the
#            model-seed placeholder (id -1, PASSWORD_HASH = 'N/A', not a BCrypt hash), so
#            it could never log in and the Development SuperAdminSeeder stayed a no-op while
#            any RoleId=4 row existed. After the approved recovery (placeholder removed;
#            the app's own SuperAdminSeeder created a working SuperAdmin from Seed:*), the
#            driver %TEMP%\opencode\s4_admin.ps1 executed them all: 39 PASS / 0 FAIL.
#            The result on each case is recorded as PASS with its driver ID.
# - Run against NEBRASDB_Step1 in Development, http://localhost:5181 (the HTTPS
#   certificate is not trusted here). Disposable users only; tokens are never printed.

### 4.3 Landlord creates a land — EXPECTED: 201
# Result: PASS (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/lands
Authorization: Bearer {{landlordToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "regionId": 2,
  "gridId": 2,
  "landNumber": "L-<stamp>",
  "village": "Village-A",
  "basin": "Basin-A",
  "parcelNumber": "P-<stamp>",
  "areaDonum": 25,
  "slopePercentage": 5,
  "distanceToGridKm": 10,
  "solarIrradiance": 6,
  "elevationM": 100
}

